  "subtitle": "A four-stitch diamond repeat on 28-count evenweave",
  "excerpt": "The diamond fill is one of the most common blackwork repeats. Four stitches form a small diamond that tiles across the fabric, creating a regular open mesh. On 28-count evenweave with two strands, the finished tile measures roughly 4 mm across.",
